<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assŭla</span></b>  (in many MSS. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">astŭla</span></b> ), ae, f.
		dim.
		axis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A splinter</i>, <i>shaving</i>, <i>chip</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">at etiam cesso foribus facere hisce assulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 1, 2, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Melandrya vocantur quercūs assulis
					similia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 15, 18, § 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">assula tenuis brevisque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 11, 22, § 54</span></i>
			. —Of marble, <i>a chip</i>, <i>shiver</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 6</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A shingle</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχίδη</span>: Bibacul. ap. <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram.
			11</span></i>.</div>
